From: Project Luma <project-luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] simple: ipa: resume autofocus with a bounded local search

Touch clients without an AfTrigger binding briefly enter manual mode and then
resume continuous autofocus to request a refocus.  Once a useful focus has
already been measured, restarting the complete sensor travel is unnecessarily
slow, visibly hunts past the subject, and makes the actuator noisy.  Preserve
the full initial scan and explicit AfTrigger semantics, but resume a mode with
the tuned local search around the current lens position.

--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
@@ -120,12 +120,14 @@ void Af::queueRequest(typename Module::Context &context,
 	const auto &afMode = controls.get(controls::AfMode);
 	if (afMode.has_value() && afMode.value() != context.activeState.knobs.af_mode) {
+		const bool haveFocus = context.configuration.focus.sharpness_max != 0;
 		context.activeState.knobs.af_mode = afMode.value();
 		LOG(IPASoftAutoFocus, Debug) << "Setting AF mode to " << afMode.value();
 
 		if (afMode.value() == controls::AfModeManual)
 			context.activeState.knobs.focus_sweep = false;
 		else
-			restart(context, false);
+			/* A resumed touch refocus must not hunt across full travel. */
+			restart(context, haveFocus);
 	}
 
 	const auto &lensPosition = controls.get(controls::LensPosition);
